    description: "Sole builds heavier than its price band implies, and the F65 is the clearest example. The 2.5-inch rollers matter here more than anywhere: at this price most competitors fit 1.9-inch rollers, which spin faster, load their bearings harder and flex the belt more tightly on every rotation. The frame took our 285 lb tester's walking sessions with no perceptible movement. Where it reaches its limit is heat — after 45 minutes of incline walking the motor housing was hot rather than warm, and while it never faltered, that is the wear mechanism that ends DC treadmills. Our judgement is that this is an excellent machine to about 260 lbs and an acceptable one to 285 if you keep sessions moderate and lubricate on the shorter interval. The 20-inch belt is the other reservation for wider users.",
  },
  {
    id: "nordictrack-commercial-1750",
    name: "NordicTrack Commercial 1750",
    category: "Best With a Screen",
    badge: "Best Console",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/s?k=NordicTrack%20Commercial%201750+Treadmill&tag=sktiger-20",
