    description: "The 1750 has the widest belt here at 22 inches, and for a heavier user that is a more meaningful specification than it sounds: a wider stance is common and a 20-inch belt produces constant small corrections to avoid the rails. The 3.5 CHP motor is the strongest DC unit on this page and held pace comfortably under our primary tester. Frame mass is ample. The constraint is the stated capacity: at 300 lbs it is the lowest here, and applying the margin we recommend throughout this guide puts its comfortable ceiling around 240 lbs. That is a real limitation for many readers of this page, and it is why a machine we rate highly elsewhere is third here. If you are within that range and guided incline sessions are what will keep you on the machine, it is an excellent choice.",
